title: Sedimentium
permalink:  2026-04-14-sedimentium
date: 2026-04-14
  
release_artist: Song of the Day  

cover:
description = Cover image, sedimentium, for the song Sedimentium
file = sedimentium.jpg
  
--synopsis  
Inspired by Andrej Karpathy's LLM wiki concept. Our dusty digital 'archives' are now acceesible again, mentored and monitored by AI agents.
--synopsis  
  
more_label: Lyrics    
    
--more  
[Verse 1]    
Floppies in boxes, CSIRO dust from '04    
Honours thesis maybe lost on a CD I can't find anymore    
PhD from '05, folders named "old comp" and "legacy"    
Fifteen years of sedimentary mind, stacked in quiet entropy    
Dropbox ghosts screaming "conflicted copy" in the night    
Tomboy notes tangled in XML, fighting for the light    
  
[Pre-Chorus]    
Layers of me, buried deep, no one left to read    
Digital sediment, waiting for a spark to breathe    
  
[Chorus]    
Sedimentium… (of minds)    
Wake the strata, let the old thoughts climb    
No bulldozer, no move, just a quiet kind of dig    
Claude in the vault, turning chaos to a bridge    
Sedimentium… mentium rising    
Decades in the rock, now alive in my fingertips    
  
[Verse 2]    
Symlinks whispering across the drive, no copy, no harm    
First do no harm — that’s the oath, keep the sedimentary calm    
Tomboy vault still breathing in its ancient XML chains    
One prompt in the dark and the whole thing starts to re-link again    
  
[Pre-Chorus]    
No more scattered drives, no more forgotten names    
AI archaeologist calling out the hidden flames    
  
[Chorus]    
Sedimentium… (of minds)    
Wake the strata, let the old thoughts climb    
No bulldozer, no move, just a gentle kind of dig    
Claude in the vault, turning chaos to a bridge    
Sedimentium… mentium rising    
Decades in the rock, now alive in my fingertips    
  
[Bridge]    
(soft, spoken almost)    
I don’t have to flatten it, I don’t have to sort    
Just point the quiet librarian at the sedimentary court    
It reads the 1989 echoes, the 2005 fire    
Weaves them back to now — no loss, no empire    
  
[Final Chorus — bigger, harmonies swelling]    
Sedimentium… (of minds)    
Every folder, every year, every buried line    
It’s all still mine, just finally intertwined    
Cognitive fingertips, the past and present aligned    
Sedimentium… mentium rising    
My whole life in one vault — finally synchronised    
  
[Outro — slow fade, single guitar]    
Sediment settles… but the mind never dies    
Sedimentium…    
(of minds)  
--more    
